```
ROLE: product_realist  VOTE: yellow
REAL_USE_CASE: Agent frameworks performing tool-result re-ingestion where (1) tool outputs are long, streamed, and front-loaded (API/JSON responses, search/RAG lists, code-execution/test output, DB query results, log tails) with actionable content in the prefix and boilerplate/pagination in the tail, (2) the next reasoning step is side-effect-free or safely reversible, and (3) rho = T_stream/T_step >= 1 (stream time dominates step generation time). Adoption requires gating to steps where wrong-commit redo cost W is bounded and reversibility holds.
OPERATIONAL_SIGNIFICANCE: Microbench-only at L0 (CPU-only analytic + Monte-Carlo trace sim, 7 seeds, N=2500/cell, stdlib-only SERIAL). Simulated realistic region (detector acc 0.7-0.8, front-load fraction f_fl 0.3-0.5) shows mean +12.1% step-latency reduction, high-rho up to +48%; 1064/1260 cells robust-win. Break-even p* = 0.07-0.39 at rho>=2 (W<=1) is low where payoff is high, inverse of EXP-0004 trap. HOWEVER real front-loading rate, real detector P(correct|fire), real rho, and real redo cost W are UNMEASURED at L0 (explicitly held). Until L1 measures corpora and detector on real partial streams, operational significance is unproven; if empirical unknowns fail, the mechanism is net-negative (blind detector -57% worst case).
ADOPTION_BARRIER: [Partial-stream detector must achieve P(correct|fire) >= p* (0.07-0.39 for rho>=2, W<=1); blind/fixed-position detector wins only 242/540 cells and loses -57% on tail-heavy/low-f_fl, proving detectability is load-bearing. Real front-loading rate of tool-result corpora unknown — L0 assumed f_fl 0.1-0.9, cannot claim real rate. Rho must be >=1 for meaningful gain; if tool results stream fast (rho<<1) the addressable win shrinks to <9%. Wrong-commit redo cost W and reversibility: side-effecting steps (tool calls, edits) imply W>1 and possible irreversibility, requiring gating early-commit to side-effect-free steps only. Engineering cost to instrument streaming, train/deploy detector, and implement rollback/re-execution on mispredict.]
RATIONALE: L0 FINDINGS (B) shows p* low (0.07-0.39) exactly in lucrative regime (rho>=2), with 1064/1260 cells robust-win and realistic-region mean +12.1% (RESULTS.md, sweep_smart.csv). L0 FINDINGS (A) proves detectability is load-bearing: blind detector wins only 242/540 cells, losing -57% worst case, while smart detector needs acc>=0.7 to clear p* in all rho>=2 cells. Packet explicitly holds claim pending L1 measurement of (1) real front-loading rate across API/JSON, search/RAG, code/test, DB, log corpora, (2) real detector P(correct|fire) and fire position d on partial streams, (3) real rho, (4) real W and reversibility (L0 FINDINGS, PRE_REG). Without those empirical measurements, the +12.1% to +48% simulated win is a microbenchmark artifact of assumed f_fl and detector accuracy; the negative result (front-loading rare or detector infeasible) is actionable guidance to NOT deploy. Prompt version: v001.
```
